<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Armon et al. (2011) Science / Efrati et al. (2009) JMPS Incompatible Shell Elasticity & Chiral Seed Pod Opening — Code-to-model traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module header maps Laws 1-5 to the Lean theorems and to Armon 2011 / Efrati 2009 / Freund 1990 / Vogel 2005 (L1-74), and each Pass 3 function docstring states its equation and Lean link (`bending_energy_prefactor` L733-741 derives B_eff from the Efrati bending content; `freund_crack_speed` L783-790; `elastic_catapult_seed_speed` L861-879). The math-KG registration lists equations 4-5 with single-range `code_locus`, `code_locus_secondary` and `lean_locus`. Deductions: the file name `2007-liang-...` and sim_id `liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening` do not match the seed paper (Armon et al. 2011) — a campaign-level identity mismatch that propagates into every audit, KG and run id (-3); the Lean theorems are Int-linear abstractions (scaled Freund speed c_R (G - Gamma), eta Delta_U partition), not statements about the ODE integration or the minimizer (-2); the \"Eq. 3 & SOM\" and \"p. 1726-1727\" pinpoints are unverified and the heuristic choices (v_arrest_frac, m/3, h_suture = h) are documented in docstrings but not traced to a source (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_065_chiral_seed_pod_opening.lean L126–L149: freund_scaled_crack_speed is c_R (G - Gamma) over Int — an abstraction of the law, not of integrate_suture_crack <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_065_chiral_seed_pod_opening.lean#L126-L149>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Armon et al. (2011) Science / Efrati et al. (2009) JMPS Incompatible Shell Elasticity & Chiral Seed Pod Opening — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The incompatible-plate core is unchanged and credited (saddle b_0 with det(b_0) = -kappa_0^2 < 0, `compute_target_curvature_tensor` L174-209; FvK critical width L210-217; L-BFGS-B minimizer of U(H, D, phi; w_tilde) L278-416). Pass 3 adds a physically coherent reduced coupling: B_eff derived from the Efrati bending content (L733-741), Delta_e -> G (L743-776), Freund's equation of motion with arrest (L783-790, L807-859), drying-driven Griffith initiation and stick-slip in `simulate_suture_fracture_ballistic_ejection` (L932-1097), and energy-partition ballistics (L861-879, L889-931), each with a negative control and backed by 2 new Lean theorems. Deductions: the pitchfork threshold is prescribed, not emergent — Lambda is normalised by (w_tilde/w_tilde_c)^4 (L324-325) so the bifurcation occurs at w_tilde_c by construction (-3); after the minimizer, H is forced to 0 for w_tilde <= w_tilde_c, its sign is forced to `branch`, and phi is snapped to 0 (L362-366), so the reported branch structure is partly post-processed (-3); e_init = kappa_0^2 assumes a perfectly flat closed valve (upper bound on stored energy, L753-756), the crack area assumes h_suture = h, c_R uses the bulk shear speed not plate waves (L778-781), and m_eff = m_seg/3 is a cantilever heuristic (L871-875) — no flexural or snap-through dynamics of the coiling valve are simulated (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py L278–L416: L-BFGS-B minimizer of the reduced non-Euclidean energy; Lambda normalised by (w_tilde/w_tilde_c)^4 at L324-325 and H/branch/phi post-processing at L362-366 make the pitchfork partly prescribed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py#L278-L416>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Armon et al. (2011) Science / Efrati et al. (2009) JMPS Incompatible Shell Elasticity & Chiral Seed Pod Opening — Morphometric validation: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1779-1944) now returns 15 measurements with references, uncertainties and tests, and the Pass 3 negative controls (kappa_0 = 0, Gamma_c >= G, achiral rings) behave correctly. Deductions are large because the remediation exposed that most references are not empirical: measurements 3-7 compare the minimizer against the `*_obs` columns of chiral_seed_pod_opening_reference.json (L48-59, L61-68), which are analytical values of the same reduced model (H_obs = (1 - nu)/2 sqrt(1 - (w_tilde_c/w_tilde)^4), tau_obs = D sin 2theta), so r = 1.0000 is self-consistency, not validation against Armon 2011 Figs. 3-4 (-10); measurement 9 uses `reference_value: 0.24` (L1877) that is the script's own computed CV 0.2405 (-4); of the six Pass 3 measurements, #10's reference is the model Gamma_c (L1888), #11's is the analytical self-estimate -tau ln(1 - sqrt(Gamma/G)) (L1898), #12's is the Freund law itself, #13's is a qualitative \"complete dehiscence\" 1.0, #14's 10 m/s is Cardamine (L1928; Bauhinia predicted 3.6x lower), and #15's is the drag-free bound (L1938) — consistency checks, not empirical morphometrics (-8). The 4-system pitch correlation (r = 0.9994) and the specimen lobe segmentation remain the only comparisons to numbers that originate outside the script." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
