<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Armon et al. (2011) Science / Efrati et al. (2009) JMPS Incompatible Shell Elasticity & Chiral Seed Pod Opening — MorphoEval overall 87.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py` (overall weighted score 87.1/100, down from 93.4 in v2). The single v2 remediation item is closed honestly as a reduced 1-D model: the Pass 2 L-BFGS-B minimizer now supplies a suture energy release rate G = B_eff (kappa_0^2 - e_final) W / h (278 J/m^2 fully dried) that drives a Freund (1990) crack equation of motion along a seeded heterogeneous suture, coupled to a desiccation curve kappa_0(t) (Griffith initiation at 63.7 h, 9 stick-slip jumps, opening fraction 1.0, <v_crack> = 0.086 c_R), an elastic-catapult launch-speed estimate (2.77 m/s) and a drag-limited ballistic range (1.65 m), with a 7-point toughness ablation that reproduces the Freund law (r = 1.0000) and a Gamma_c >= G no-fracture control. Two new Lean 4 theorems (5 laws, 0 sorrys) and 4 new self-test checks (12/12) were added. The score falls because the remediation exposed that the v2 \"observations\" were analytical outputs of the same model, the specimen-CV reference is the script's own value, the pitchfork threshold is an input rather than emergent, and every Pass 3 fracture/ballistic constant is an unsourced modelling choice benchmarked against a different taxon. Overall 87.1/100 (faithfulness 85.3, reproducibility 91.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 45670cb8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 94, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 95. Output judged: docs/media/chiral_seed_pod_opening_comparison.png: rendered output of 2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py at 45670cb8, image/png, 1277872 B, 2775×2460 px, artifact_sha256 172e958f57c4f16dd8b2e082fc2efb5442a52bdf87f09ac52a5d36928b1c4960 (sha256 172e958f57c4f16dd8b2e082fc2efb5442a52bdf87f09ac52a5d36928b1c4960), spec_fingerprint 988d946ef567ff70b70ecbbb7abf3522d31bdbaab73fbfe18f6b573345ff5c32. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 988d946ef567ff70b70ecbbb7abf3522d31bdbaab73fbfe18f6b573345ff5c32; artifact_sha256: 172e958f57c4f16dd8b2e082fc2efb5442a52bdf87f09ac52a5d36928b1c4960; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/bauhinia_chiral_seed_pod_specimen.jpg=047f357961bc58c5..., datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/chiral_seed_pod_opening_reference.json=4b1fa5df06327c65..., datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/paper_citations.bib=41f9ca2ead3c8d74..., datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/scout_manifest.json=05711e5e7df6cb17..., datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/suture_fracture_ballistic_reference.json=fc8fab08281dd6e0...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-chiral-seed-pod-opening-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Armon et al. (2011): orthogonal +-45 deg sclerenchyma layers prescribe a saddle target curvature b_0 = diag(kappa_0, -kappa_0) with det(b_0) < 0; narrow strips (w_tilde below a critical FvK width) adopt pure-twist helicoids, wide strips cylindrical helical ribbons; cutting angle controls chirality and pitch | Efrati et al. (2009): incompatible non-Euclidean plate energy E = E_stretch + E_bend with bending content proportional to Y h^3 [nu Tr(M)^2 + (1 - nu) Tr(M^2)], M = b - b_0 | Freund (1990): mode-I dynamic energy release rate G_dyn(v) ~ (1 - v/c_R) G, so a crack runs at v = c_R (1 - Gamma_c/G) and arrests when Gamma_c >= G | Hofhuis et al. (2016) / Swaine & Beer (1977) / Vogel (2005): explosive seed launch speeds of order 10 m/s (Cardamine) and 70 m/s (Hura), elastic-catapult energy budgets and drag-limited ranges of small projectiles; reconstructed_in_script: Reduced L-BFGS-B non-Euclidean energy functional U(H, D, phi; w_tilde) over the dimensionless width, pitchfork sweep, cutting-angle sweep, 4-system table, 3-D ribbon mesh and specimen segmentation (Pass 2); Pass 3 adds B_eff Delta_e -> suture G, a 1-D Freund crack equation of motion over a seeded heterogeneous toughness field, drying-coupled Griffith initiation and stick-slip propagation, an elastic-catapult launch-speed estimate and an RK4 quadratic-drag trajectory, and a 7-point Gamma_c/G ablation sweep; transfer_boundary: The `*_obs` columns of the width and cutting-angle sweep tables in chiral_seed_pod_opening_reference.json are analytical values of the same reduced model (H_obs = (1 - nu)/2 sqrt(1 - (w_tilde_c/w_tilde)^4), tau_obs = D sin 2theta), not digitised Armon 2011 figure points; the r = 1.0000 correlations are self-consistency, not validation | The launch-speed benchmark (10 m/s) is Cardamine hirsuta and the upper bound (70 m/s) is Hura crepitans; no Bauhinia variegata launch-speed, suture-toughness or dispersal datum was verifiable offline, and the predicted 2.8-3.8 m/s is ~3.6x below the Cardamine value | All 12 fracture/ballistic constants (rho, Gamma_c, CV_Gamma, a_0, tau_dry, n_seeds, m_seed, r_seed, C_d, eta, launch angle, launch height) are `provenance: model` in suture_fracture_ballistic_reference.json; does_not_claim: 3-D elastodynamic shell or FEM simulation of valve coiling (inertia enters only via eta and a first-mode cantilever coil time), plate-wave corrections to c_R, a measured Bauhinia fracture toughness or seed mass, or digitised comparison against Armon 2011 Figs. 3-4." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py:1175 and 1194-1200 — the specimen ROI is hard-coded and the upper/lower valve assignment uses `runs[0]`/`runs[-1]`; expose the ROI in the JSON with provenance, make the valve assignment robust to the number of runs, and overlay the specimen outline on Panel A so the 3-D mesh heuristic (cup = 0.5 kappa_t T^2, L479) is checked visually.",
        "remediation needed: 2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py:324-325 and 362-366 — Lambda is normalised by (w_tilde/w_tilde_c)^4 so the pitchfork is at w_tilde_c by construction, and H / branch sign / phi are post-processed after the minimizer. Derive Lambda from the unnormalised FvK stretching coefficient so w_tilde_c is emergent, remove the H = 0 and sign forcing, and update the SHA-pinned JSON `reduced_non_euclidean_energy_density` (L33) to the form the code actually minimises.",
        "remediation needed: 2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py:861-887 and 932-1097 — ejection speed is an eta energy partition with a cantilever m/3 heuristic and a first-mode coil time; no flexural or snap-through dynamics of the coiling valve are simulated. Add valve coiling elastodynamics (Kirchhoff rod or shallow-shell with inertia, Forterre 2005 style snap-through) so v_seed emerges from the dynamics rather than from eta, and replace the bulk-shear c_R (L778-781) with plate-wave speeds.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/chiral_seed_pod_opening_reference.json:48-68 with 2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py:1811-1861 — the `*_obs` columns of the width and cutting-angle sweeps are analytical values of the same reduced model, so measurements 3-7 (r = 1.0000) are self-referential. Replace them with digitised Armon 2011 Fig. 3-4 points (plot-digitiser coordinates, axis calibration and provenance recorded in the JSON) and re-pin the SHA-256; drop or re-source the specimen-CV reference 0.24 at L1877, which is the script's own output.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/paper_citations.bib:49-92 — the four new DOIs (Freund 1990, Hofhuis 2016, Swaine & Beer 1977, Vogel 2005) are flagged unverified offline and the \"~10 m/s\" / \"~70 m/s\" values are recalled; verify the DOIs online, digitise the launch-speed figures with page pinpoints, and either use Forterre 2005 (header L19-22) in a computation or drop it from `source_refs`.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/suture_fracture_ballistic_reference.json:29-50 and 2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py:1882-1943 — all 12 fracture/ballistic constants are `provenance: model` and the launch-speed benchmark (L1928, 10 m/s) is Cardamine hirsuta. Source or measure Bauhinia variegata suture toughness, seed mass and a launch-speed / dispersal-kernel datum (high-speed video or field dispersal) and replace the transfer-boundary references; cite the Y = 420 MPa default (JSON L27)." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.71e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Armon et al. (2011) Science / Efrati et al. (2009) JMPS Incompatible Shell Elasticity & Chiral Seed Pod Opening — Parameter expressivity: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 sweeps are retained (11-point w_tilde pitchfork L497-576, 7-point cutting angle L577-644, 4 systems L645-722). Pass 3 adds the 7-point Gamma_c/G in {0.2..1.2} ablation with homogeneous vs heterogeneous suture and a Gamma_c >= G no-fracture negative control (`evaluate_suture_toughness_sweep` L1098-1162), the desiccation trajectory kappa_0(t) as a swept driver (L932-1097), eta-scaling of the launch speed checked in the self-test, and new CLI overrides `--gamma-c`, `--eta`, `--m-seed` plus a `--fracture-json` summary mode (L2079-2082, L2103-2109), all wired into the simulation. Deductions: CV_Gamma, a_0, tau_dry, launch angle and height are fixed JSON constants with no CLI or sweep (-3); the opening fraction near Gamma_c ~ G is set by the numerical arrest threshold `v_arrest_frac = 0.01` (L815, L831), which is not exposed or swept (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py L807–L835: v_arrest_frac = 0.01 numerical arrest threshold sets opening fraction near Gamma_c ~ G; not exposed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py#L807-L835>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Armon et al. (2011) Science / Efrati et al. (2009) JMPS Incompatible Shell Elasticity & Chiral Seed Pod Opening — Reproducibility package: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`self_test()` (L1946-2067) runs 12 checks in 2.3 s: 8 Pass 2 checks plus energy bookkeeping, Freund law and arrest, drying-coupled dehiscence + catapult + ballistics + no-fracture control + eta-scaling, and toughness sweep + two-run determinism; SHA-256 verification is fail-closed; the default render completes in ~8.5 s and writes the 9-panel PNG, the fracture PNG and both GIFs (`main` L2069-2121); `--fracture-json` emits a machine-readable summary. Deductions: the drying grid (96 points, ~4.5 h) sets the t_c resolution and is not a CLI parameter (-2); the growth GIF is byte-identical to the committed version and does not reflect Pass 3, and Panel I's legend overlaps the Hura label (-2); the PNG outputs are gitignored so the rendered figures are not versioned (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "docs/media/chiral_seed_pod_opening_growth.gif (generated output, not in repo): 12-frame growth GIF regenerated by the default run; byte-identical to the committed Pass 2 version (Pass 3 did not change it) — docs/media/chiral_seed_pod_opening_growth.gif: rendered output of 2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py at 45670cb8, image/gif, 236086 B, 608×456 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 ab3bfe47b66182ba264e6aeaf3e791ae9649f6460e2c4fa9006787dbf84b2910 (sha256 ab3bfe47b66182ba264e6aeaf3e791ae9649f6460e2c4fa9006787dbf84b2910), spec_fingerprint 988d946ef567ff70b70ecbbb7abf3522d31bdbaab73fbfe18f6b573345ff5c32" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-repro-package-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-repro-package-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Armon et al. (2011) Science / Efrati et al. (2009) JMPS Incompatible Shell Elasticity & Chiral Seed Pod Opening — Source and data traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Five dataset files are SHA-256-pinned and verified fail-closed at runtime (`EXPECTED_SHA256` L106-127, `verify_dataset_integrity` L137-150), including the new `suture_fracture_ballistic_reference.json` whose every constant carries a `provenance` flag (source / derived / model) and an explicit honesty note (JSON L9), and `paper_citations.bib` gains Freund 1990, Hofhuis 2016, Swaine & Beer 1977 and Vogel 2005 with the offline-unverified status recorded in each `note` (bib L47-92). Deductions: 12 of the Pass 3 constants are `provenance: model` (rho, Gamma_c, CV_Gamma, a_0, tau_dry, n_seeds, m_seed, r_seed, C_d, eta, angle, height; JSON L29, L37-39, L41, L44-50) and Y = 420 MPa is inherited from the Pass 2 JSON default with no table citation (JSON L27) (-5); the four new DOIs could not be verified offline (-3); the bilayer formula's \"p. 1726-1727\" attribution and the w_tilde_c formula's \"Eq. 3 & SOM\" attribution are unverified, and the Pass 2 calibration Delta_eps = 0.0266 (L161, L1789) is chosen so that 1.5 * 0.0266 / 0.095 = 0.42 exactly (-3); Forterre 2005 is cited in the header (L19-22) and bib but used in no computation (-2); the SHA-pinned reference JSON still shows the un-normalised energy density (JSON L33) while the code uses the w_tilde_c-normalised form (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py L160–L173: compute_sclerenchyma_bilayer_kappa0 default Delta_eps = 0.0266 reproduces kappa_0 = 0.42 exactly; attribution of the 3/2 bilayer formula unverified <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py#L160-L173>",
        "datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/chiral_seed_pod_opening_reference.json L70–L123: 4-system table with page/figure pointers only; no digitisation coordinates for Erythrina or latex R_obs/P_obs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/chiral_seed_pod_opening_reference.json#L70-L123>",
        "datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/suture_fracture_ballistic_reference.json L9–L52: Honesty note and per-constant provenance flags; 12 constants are provenance: model, Y = 420 MPa inherits an uncited Pass 2 default <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/suture_fracture_ballistic_reference.json#L9-L52>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-source-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Armon et al. (2011) Science / Efrati et al. (2009) JMPS Incompatible Shell Elasticity & Chiral Seed Pod Opening — Morphological realism / specimen match: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The SHA-256-locked Bauhinia variegata specimen (MHNT.BOT.2011.3.22) is still segmented into both dehisced valves and 8 helical lobe apices (`segment_bauhinia_pod_specimen` L1163-1248) and Panel E overlays the segmentation on the photograph; the 9-panel figure now adds suture-crack, catapult and ballistic panels (G-I, `_draw_fracture_panels` L1249-1358) and a 45-frame fracture GIF (L1666-1778). Deductions: the ROI `x0, y0, x1, y1 = 150, 60, 928, 452` is hard-coded (L1175) and the upper/lower valve assignment relies on `runs[0]`/`runs[-1]` column logic (L1194-1200), which is brittle (-3); the 4-system table's Erythrina and latex R_obs/P_obs carry only \"p. 1726\"/\"Fig. 2 & 3\" pointers with no digitisation coordinates and the Bauhinia R_obs = 3.39 cm vs sim 3.396 cm suggests back-computation (`evaluate_pod_and_mimetic_specimens` L645-722; JSON L70-123) (-4); the new fracture/ballistic panels compare against Cardamine and Hura (different taxa) because no Bauhinia launch-speed or dispersal specimen datum exists in the package (-4); Panel A has no specimen overlay and the 3-D mesh cup = 0.5 kappa_t T^2 and helix frame (L466-479) are unvalidated visual heuristics (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py L645–L722: 4-system table evaluation; the JSON R_obs/P_obs for Erythrina and latex carry page pointers only, no digitisation coordinates <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py#L645-L722>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-specimen-match-1>,
